{"name":"Trick or Treat","hex":"#eab38a","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"trick or treat","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Interjection","definitions":["A form of a light-hearted request by which children obtain candy on Halloween while wearing themed costumes."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/trick_or_treat"}],"entries":[{"title":"Trick or Treat (1986 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Trick or Treat is a 1986 American supernatural horror film directed by Charles Martin Smith in his directorial debut, and produced and released by De Laurentiis Entertainment Group. It stars Marc Price and Tony Fields, with special appearances by Gene Simmons and Ozzy Osbourne in his film debut. The plot centers on an outcast metalhead teenager who is haunted by the ghost of his rock hero."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/4/45/Trick_or_Treat_%281986_film%29_Poster.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trick_or_Treat_(1986_film)","wikidata":"Q1650965"},{"title":"Trick or Treat (band)","blocks":[{"text":"Trick or Treat is an Italian power metal band formed in 2002 in Modena. The group's line-up has been mostly the same since its inception, except for the drummer position, which underwent changes in 2006 and 2011, and in 2014 guitarist and founding member Luca Cabri left the band and was replaced by Luca Venturelli."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trick_or_Treat_(band)","wikidata":"Q3663292"},{"title":"Trick-or-treating","blocks":[{"text":"Trick-or-treating is a traditional Halloween custom for children and adults in some countries. During the evening of Halloween, on the night between 31 October and 1 November, people in costumes travel from house to house, asking for treats with the phrase \"trick or treat\". The \"treat\" is some form of confectionery, usually candy/sweets, although in some cultures money is given instead. The \"trick\" refers to a threat, usually idle, to perform mischief on the resident(s) or their property if no treat is given. Some people signal that they are willing to hand out treats by putting up Halloween decorations outside their doors; houses may also leave their porch lights on as a universal indicator that they have candy; some simply leave treats available on their porches for the children to take freely, on the honour system."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/41/Trick_or_Treater.jpg/330px-Trick_or_Treater.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trick-or-treating","wikidata":"Q47195"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/Souling_on_Halloween.png/250px-Souling_on_Halloween.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/e/e3/Souling_on_Halloween.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/Souling_on_Halloween.png/250px-Souling_on_Halloween.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"\"A soul-cake, a soul-cake, have mercy on all Christian souls for a soul-cake.\" — a popular English souling rhyme[10]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASouling_on_Halloween.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/Halloween_Shop%2C_Derry%2C_September_2010_%2802%29.JPG/500px-Halloween_Shop%2C_Derry%2C_September_2010_%2802%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/Halloween_Shop%2C_Derry%2C_September_2010_%2802%29.JPG/1280px-Halloween_Shop%2C_Derry%2C_September_2010_%2802%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/Halloween_Shop%2C_Derry%2C_September_2010_%2802%29.JPG/500px-Halloween_Shop%2C_Derry%2C_September_2010_%2802%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Halloween shop in Derry, Northern Ireland. Halloween masks are called ‘false faces’ in Ireland and Scotland.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHalloween_Shop%2C_Derry%2C_September_2010_(02).JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/Waterdown_Public_School%2C_Ontario%2C_1928_halloween_costume.jpg/500px-Waterdown_Public_School%2C_Ontario%2C_1928_halloween_costume.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/Waterdown_Public_School%2C_Ontario%2C_1928_halloween_costume.jpg/500px-Waterdown_Public_School%2C_Ontario%2C_1928_halloween_costume.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Girl in a Halloween costume in 1928 in Ontario, Canada, the same province where the Scottish Halloween custom of \"guising\" is first recorded in North America","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWaterdown_Public_School%2C_Ontario%2C_1928_halloween_costume.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Trick_or_Treating_-_Beaumont%2C_California_%281950%29.png/500px-Trick_or_Treating_-_Beaumont%2C_California_%281950%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Trick_or_Treating_-_Beaumont%2C_California_%281950%29.png/500px-Trick_or_Treating_-_Beaumont%2C_California_%281950%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Newspaper clipping of kids trick-or-treating in Beaumont in 1950","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATrick_or_Treating_-_Beaumont%2C_California_(1950).png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b9/A